---
import Showcase from '../layouts/Showcase.astro';
---
<Showcase title="helmstudio · Wire the models. Direct the film." description="A self-hosted studio for images, video, voices, music and sound on your own Mac and NVIDIA machines, with an assistant that works every screen and Magic, a board that lays out the film in time.">
<div class="wrap">
  <header class="hero" id="top">
    <a class="alpha-pill" href="/start/whats-new/"><b>Alpha</b> <span class="long">Early software: expect changes · </span>What's new →</a>
    <p class="eyebrow">Self-hosted AI studio · Apple Silicon and NVIDIA</p>
    <h1>Wire the models.<br><span class="grad">Direct the film.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Images, video with sound, voices, music and sound effects from open models, on machines you own. An Assistant that works every screen with you, and Magic, a board where the whole film takes shape in time.</p>
    <div class="ctas">
      <a class="btn primary" href="#start">Install helmstudio →</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/assistant/">Meet the Assistant</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/magic/">See Magic</a>
    </div>
    <div class="models" aria-label="Model families">
      <span>Qwen Image 2.1</span><span>MiniMax H3 Image</span><span>LTX-2.5</span><span>MiniMax H3</span><span>Qwen3-TTS</span><span>ZONOS3</span><span>MiniMax Music 3</span><span>ACE-Step 1.5</span><span>Stable Audio 3</span><span>MMAudio</span><span>Qwen3.8</span>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-shot" style="margin-inline:0">
      <div class="window"><div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <img src="/screens/assistant-create.jpg" alt="Create with the Assistant drawer: it has written the prompt, set the model to Qwen Image Turbo, added @mara and Blue hour lighting, and asks before generating 4 images">
      </div>
    </figure>
  </header>
</div>

<section class="stage" id="assistant" aria-labelledby="assistant-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="stage-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The Assistant</p>
      <h2 id="assistant-h">A co-director that <span class="grad">works the screen</span> with you.</h2>
      <p>Say what you want in a sentence. The Assistant opens the right screen, picks the model, writes the prompt and sets the look. You watch every change land, with Undo on each one. It never spends GPU time without asking.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-shot" style="margin:40px 0 0">
      <div class="window"><div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <video src="/screens/assistant-scroll.mp4" poster="/screens/assistant-scroll.jpg" width="2240" height="1292" autoplay muted loop playsinline preload="metadata" aria-label="A real session in helmstudio: the Assistant plans a short film, makes the fisherman's character sheet, saves the look and makes keyframe 1, while the first clip plays on the stage"></video>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="cap">A real session · one sentence became a film plan, a character sheet, a saved look and the first keyframe</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ol class="flow">
      <li><b>Ask</b><span>"Make a rainy London evening still of @mara, cinematic."</span></li>
      <li><b>It does the work</b><span>Opens Create, sets Qwen Image Turbo, writes the prompt, adds Blue hour. Each step can be undone.</span></li>
      <li><b>It asks first</b><span>A card shows the model, size, seeds, the host and the time it will take. You press Generate.</span></li>
      <li><b>Steer it live</b><span>Type while it works. "Use Turbo instead" is read at the next step, and it changes course.</span></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="chips" aria-label="What the Assistant does">
      <span class="chip">Sees the screen you are on</span>
      <span class="chip">Looks at your takes</span>
      <span class="chip">Listens to sound and voices</span>
      <span class="chip">Knows every model's settings</span>
      <span class="chip">Builds Magic boards</span>
      <span class="chip">Asks before costly runs</span>
      <span class="chip">Undo on every step</span>
      <span class="chip">Remembers what you like</span>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:24px"><a class="btn" href="/assistant/">More about the Assistant →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="stage" id="magic" aria-labelledby="magic-h">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="stage-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Magic</p>
      <h2 id="magic-h">The whole film, <span class="grad">laid out in time.</span></h2>
      <p>Lanes for the storyboard, the shots, the voices, the music and the sound, on one ruler. Every block is a generation with its own preview and status. Run what is out of date, pick the best takes, then export the film or send it to the Timeline.</p>
    </div>
    <figure class="hero-shot" style="margin:40px 0 0">
      <div class="window"><div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <img src="/screens/magic-director.jpg" alt="A Magic board, Ink and the Sunflower, with the Assistant beside it. Asked to listen to the music, it reports per cue: Cue A has a woman singing in a wordless film and stops mid-phrase; Cue C opens with a hum and ends on a harsh chord; each with a fix" loading="lazy">
      </div>
      <figcaption class="cap">A real board · the Assistant listened to the music and says what to fix in each cue</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <ol class="flow">
      <li><b>Add at a point</b><span>Click a lane at a time and pick a shot, a still, a line, a cue, a sound or a storyboard frame.</span></li>
      <li><b>Fill the request</b><span>The same few fields for every model of a kind. Each model's own settings wait under Advanced.</span></li>
      <li><b>Run and pick</b><span>Run a block, a lane or the board, with the GPU time shown first. Pin the take you like.</span></li>
      <li><b>Export</b><span>One button makes the MP4, or send the board to the Timeline as a new sequence. The board stays as it is.</span></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="chips" aria-label="What Magic does">
      <span class="chip">Characters, props and places as assets</span>
      <span class="chip">Storyboard frames to shots</span>
      <span class="chip">Voice and music tied to shots</span>
      <span class="chip">Fades, crossfades and ducking</span>
      <span class="chip">Cut, dissolve, fade, wipe and morph</span>
      <span class="chip">Snapshots and history</span>
      <span class="chip">A director Assistant that plans first</span>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:24px"><a class="btn" href="/magic/">More about Magic →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="wrap">
  <section class="rooms" id="rooms" aria-label="Tour">
    <article class="room">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Create</p>
        <h3>One screen for every image, clip, voice, song and sound.</h3>
        <p>Pick a kind and a model, write a prompt, make takes. Image, Video, Voice, Music and Sound sit side by side, and your prompt stays when you switch.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Presets from Draft to Final, with time and peak memory before you run</li>
          <li>Songs with lyrics, and sound effects matched to a video</li>
          <li>The same workflow as a form or as a node graph</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/studio/create/">Read the Create guide →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="window"><div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><img src="/screens/create.jpg" alt="Create with Qwen Image: live preview at step 12 of 40, presets, references, canvas, quality and LoRA panels" loading="lazy"></div>
    </article>

    <article class="room flip">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Gallery</p>
        <h3>Every take remembers how it was made.</h3>
        <p>Prompt, model, seed, size and inputs travel with each take. Send any of them back to work in one click.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Lineage: what a take was made from and where it was used</li>
          <li>Use in… Animate, Edit, Extend or Retake</li>
          <li>Save as an element, a look or a pipeline</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/studio/gallery/">Read the Gallery guide →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="window"><div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><img src="/screens/gallery.jpg" alt="Gallery grid with filters and the side panel showing how the selected take was made and its Use in actions" loading="lazy"></div>
    </article>

    <article class="room">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Timeline</p>
        <h3>Cut the film where you make it.</h3>
        <p>Direct new shots in the gaps, retake a section, add voice lines, and export one MP4.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>A new shot can start from the last frame of the one before</li>
          <li>The sequence's cast and look apply to every shot</li>
          <li>Export copies streams when it can, re-encodes when it must</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/studio/timeline/">Read the Timeline guide →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="window"><div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><img src="/screens/timeline.jpg" alt="Timeline with five shots, a new shot being composed in a gap, and clip actions for Extend, Retake and Replace" loading="lazy"></div>
    </article>

    <article class="room flip">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Pipelines</p>
        <h3>Batches that check their own work.</h3>
        <p>Run a workflow over a list while you are away. A judge looks at each take against your checklist, keeps the best and sends the rest back.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>It suggests first; switch to auto when you trust it</li>
          <li>It learns from the takes you keep and reject</li>
          <li>Every retry is capped and logged</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/studio/pipelines/">Read the Pipelines guide →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="window"><div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><img src="/screens/judge.jpg" alt="Judge review: the judge suggests take 3 as clean and sharp, with checklist chips and the pipeline's memory of past picks" loading="lazy"></div>
    </article>

    <article class="room">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Models</p>
        <h3>Every model, every machine, one place.</h3>
        <p>See each family's variants and add-ons and which machine has them. Admins download weights to the machine, and the folder, that needs them.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Base, Turbo, Distilled, and smaller fp8 weights for NVIDIA</li>
          <li>Several model folders per machine, such as an external drive</li>
          <li>A LoRA library for everyone</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/models/">Browse the models →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="window"><div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><img src="/screens/models.jpg" alt="Models: Qwen Image 2.1 variants with sizes and hosts, optional add-ons, and the components panel" loading="lazy"></div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="machines" aria-labelledby="machines-h">
    <div class="duo" style="margin-top:0">
      <div class="copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Your machines</p>
        <h3 id="machines-h">Runs where your GPUs are.</h3>
        <p>Each run goes to a machine with the weights and the memory, or to the one you pick. Nothing you make leaves your machines.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="window"><div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><img src="/screens/run-on.jpg" alt="Run on menu: Auto or a named host, with hosts that cannot take the run greyed out with the reason" loading="lazy"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="specs">
      <div class="spec"><small>Apple Silicon</small><b>MLX, PyTorch and native</b><span>Runners share one memory budget on each Mac.</span></div>
      <div class="spec"><small>NVIDIA</small><b>One server or many</b><span>PyTorch and native runners, with smaller fp8 and int8 weights.</span></div>
      <div class="spec"><small>Your team</small><b>Private per person</b><span>Each user sees only their own takes, boards, sessions and pipelines.</span></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="close" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-h">
    <p class="eyebrow">Install, then sign in</p>
    <h2 id="start-h">Your studio is <span class="grad">one download away.</span></h2>
    <div class="term"><pre><span class="c"># Mac: the app, no Docker needed</span>
<span class="p">$</span> open helmstudio-0.1.0-alpha.6.dmg
<span class="c"># Windows and Linux: Docker and the release's compose.yml</span>
<span class="p">$</span> docker compose up -d --wait</pre></div>
    <div class="ctas">
      <a class="btn primary" href="/start/install/">Read the install guide →</a>
      <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/janishar/helmstudio">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
</Showcase>
